{#-
  Everything a rendered file needs to know about `upstream_source`.

  Each template that writes an upstream pin, a link to an upstream release or
  the dependency policy for upstream sources imports it from here, so a new
  source is one more branch in each macro below rather than a search through
  the template. The scripts have their counterpart in
  `template/scripts/src/upstream_source.dart.jinja`, and the two must agree:
  what `dependency` writes into rust/Cargo.toml is what `pinFrom` reads back
  and `rewriteCargoToml` rewrites.

  This file lives outside `template/` on purpose. Copier resolves imports from
  the template repository's root, not from `_subdirectory`, and nothing outside
  `_subdirectory` is ever copied — so it is available to every template and
  reaches no generated project. Import it with context:

    {% from "macros/upstream.jinja" import dependency with context %}

  `upstream_source` is read with a default because copier leaves a skipped
  question's variable to its default, and every project generated before the
  question existed is a `git_tag` project.
-#}

{#- The source's answer, `git_tag` when the question was never asked. -#}
{%- macro source() -%}
{{- upstream_source | default('git_tag') -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The crate whose version `upstream_version` records. -#}
{%- macro primary() -%}
{{- upstream_crates.split(',')[0] | trim -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The requirement `upstream_crate_versions` records for `crate`. -#}
{%- macro crate_requirement(crate) -%}
{%- for entry in (upstream_crate_versions | default('')).split(',') | map('trim') | select -%}
{%- if (entry.split('=', 1)[0] | trim) == crate -%}
{{- entry.split('=', 1)[1] | trim -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#-
  The value of `<crate> = …` in rust/Cargo.toml.

  git_tag: every upstream crate from native_repo at the one tag.
  crates_io: the primary crate pinned exactly — the update check reads the
  current release from it, and a range would leave that to Cargo.lock — and
  every other crate at the requirement the primary itself declares.
-#}
{%- macro dependency(crate) -%}
{%- if source() == 'crates_io' -%}
{%- if crate == primary() -%}
"={{ upstream_version }}"
{%- else -%}
"{{ crate_requirement(crate) }}"
{%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
{ git = "https://github.com/{{ native_repo }}", tag = "{{ upstream_version }}" }
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#-
  The pin as a bare version, for display: `v1.2.3` reads `1.2.3`.

  For git_tag this must stay in step with `GitTagSource.semverOf` in
  upstream_source.dart, which rewrites the README badge on every bump: strip
  `version_tag_prefix`, and fall back to a bare `v`/`V` when the tag does not
  carry it. Sliced rather than `replace`d — `replace` would cut the prefix
  wherever it occurs, not only at the front.
-#}
{%- macro version() -%}
{%- if not upstream_version -%}
1.0.0
{%- elif source() == 'crates_io' -%}
{{- upstream_version -}}
{%- elif version_tag_prefix and upstream_version.startswith(version_tag_prefix) -%}
{{- upstream_version[version_tag_prefix | length:] -}}
{%- elif upstream_version[:1] in ['v', 'V'] -%}
{{- upstream_version[1:] -}}
{%- else -%}
{{- upstream_version -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#-
  A page about the upstream release `pin`, which may be a shell expression such
  as `${NATIVE_VERSION}`: the GitHub release for a tag, the crates.io page for a
  registry version. Must agree with `pageFor` in upstream_source.dart.
-#}
{%- macro release_page(pin) -%}
{%- if source() == 'crates_io' -%}
https://crates.io/crates/{{ primary() }}/{{ pin }}
{%- else -%}
https://github.com/{{ native_repo }}/releases/tag/{{ pin }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#-
  An example pin for `version` in the form this source pins by, for commands
  quoted in documentation: `v1.0.0` for a `v` prefix, `1.0.0` from a registry.
  A pin of the wrong shape is refused by the scripts, so an example that has
  one does not work when copied.
-#}
{%- macro example_pin(version='1.0.0') -%}
{%- if source() == 'crates_io' -%}
{{- version -}}
{%- else -%}
{{- version_tag_prefix | default('v') -}}{{- version -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- What the link to `release_page` is, in prose. -#}
{%- macro release_label() -%}
{%- if source() == 'crates_io' -%}
page on crates.io
{%- else -%}
release notes
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- What a pin is called in prose: a `tag`, or a crates.io `version`. -#}
{%- macro pin_noun() -%}
{%- if source() == 'crates_io' -%}
version
{%- else -%}
tag
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#-
  The git repository the upstream crates are fetched from, or nothing when the
  source is not a git one — rust/deny.toml allows exactly this, so a registry
  source leaves no git source allowed for upstream.
-#}
{%- macro git_url() -%}
{%- if upstream_crates and source() == 'git_tag' -%}
https://github.com/{{ native_repo }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
